+### 3.2 the inverse partial layer — computed and run
+
+the argument for 16 inverse rounds was degree: x^(p−2) has degree p − 2,
+so sixteen rounds "give" (p − 2)^16. an attacker never meets that degree.
+carry the state as rational functions of one free input X with a common
+denominator, x_i = N_i / D. a full x⁷ round maps (N_i + cD)^7 / D^7 and
+multiplies the degree by 7; an inverse round on x_0 maps
+x_0 ↦ D / (N_0 + cD), and with the common denominator D · U
+(U = N_0 + cD) the numerators become D², N_i U: the degree doubles. the
+whole permutation is therefore a rational function of degree at most
+7^8 · 2^16 = 377 801 998 336 ≈ 2^38.46 in any single input limb, on all
+inputs except the ≤ 16 · D² roots of some inverse argument (probability
+negligible). the Poseidon paper rejected inverse partial rounds for exactly
+this growth (ePrint 2019/458: "the inverse function does not provide a sufficiently fast degree growth"; its x⁻¹ interpolation bound counts one bit of degree per partial round); hemera#2 derived the
+same bound (`research/full-round-status.md`).
+
+`audit/campaign/cico1.py` builds N_limb − target · D symbolically with the
+real constants and matrices, takes gcd(f, X^p − X) by one modular powering,
+reads off the roots, and checks every root on the concrete permutation
+(`hemera_ref.py`, itself checked against the vectors). capacity fixed to a
+hash's final block (length 168), seven rate limbs fixed at random values,
+X in limb 3, target output limb 0 = 0. one core of an M4 Max, python-flint
+0.9.0, 2026-10-16:
+
+| R_F | R_P (x⁻¹) | degree bound | degree found | total time | roots | verified on the permutation |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 + 1 | 4 | 784 = 2^9.61 | 784 | 0.1 s | 1 | 1 |
+| 1 + 1 | 8 | 12 544 = 2^13.61 | 12 544 | 0.2 s | 2 | 2 |
+| 1 + 1 | 10 | 50 176 = 2^15.61 | 50 176 | 0.8 s | 1 | 1 |
+| 2 + 2 | 4 | 38 416 = 2^15.23 | 38 416 | 0.6 s | 1 | 1 |
+| 1 + 1 | 12 | 200 704 = 2^17.61 | 200 704 | 3.9 s | 0 | — |
+| 2 + 2 | 8 | 614 656 = 2^19.23 | 614 656 | 13.7 s | 0 | — |
+| 1 + 1 | 14 | 802 816 = 2^19.61 | 802 816 | 22.1 s | 1 | 1 |
+| 3 + 3 | 4 | 1 882 384 = 2^20.84 | 1 882 384 | 45.8 s | 0 | — |
+| 1 + 1 | 16 (all) | 3 211 264 = 2^21.61 | 3 211 264 | 92.1 s | 1 | 1 |
+| 2 + 2 | 10 | 2 458 624 = 2^21.23 | 2 458 624 | 120.2 s | 1 | 1 |
+
+the bound is attained exactly every time: no cancellation saves the
+defender. a run with no root is the expected ~37 % case of a random
+polynomial; the attacker changes one fixed limb and repeats. time grows as
+D^1.0 to D^1.2 over the measured range (2^17.6 → 2^21.6; the machine was
+shared, so single runs carry noise). extrapolated to the full 0.3
+permutation, D = 2^38.46 is 2^16.85 times the largest run: 92 s · 2^16.85
+to 92 s · 2^20.2, i.e. 10^7 to 10^8 core-seconds (0.35 to 3.5
+core-years) of fast-polynomial arithmetic, ≈ 2^52–2^56 field multiplications, with
+polynomials of 2^38.46 coefficients (2.75 TB each, order 10 TB working
+memory). the generic cost of the same CICO-1 problem is 2^64 permutation
+calls: ≈ 4.7 · 10^5 core-years at the batched 0.80 µs per permutation.
+memory, not time, is the barrier, and out-of-core NTT arithmetic over
+Goldilocks is an engineering problem with known solutions (§3.4).
+
+what this does and does not break. it is a full-round distinguisher of the
+0.3 permutation and an attack on its one-limb CICO problem at 2^19 to 2^23
+below generic; it falsifies "hemera's permutation as an ideal permutation"
+as a model. it is not a collision or preimage of the 32-byte digest
+(§3.1). it does not reach the chain's proof of work: the 168-byte header
+occupies three full blocks, so every header byte passes through at least
+two permutations before the output (degree D² > p), and sponge rate limbs
+are confined to 2^56 values (a random root is encodable with probability
+2^-8). its reach into the zheng rows that treat the permutation as ideal
+is open (review question R4).
+
+with x⁷ in the partial rounds the same construction multiplies the degree
+by 7 per partial round, and the x⁷-only Poseidon2 reference (R_F 8, R_P
+22) already has 7^30 = 2^84.2 > p; v2 has 7^60. the univariate route is
+closed for both.
